220409589	730	Hello Valve,\n\nI want to provide feedback on the recent reload update in Counter-Strike 2.\n\nThe intention to increase strategic depth is understandable. However, the current implementation feels like it prioritizes theoretical depth over actual gameplay experience.\n\nThe system introduces punishment without creating meaningful decision-making. Losing all remaining ammunition on reload does not encourage strategy—it simply discourages natural gameplay habits that were previously part of optimal play.\n\nAdditionally, this change feels more like artificial difficulty than a skill-based challenge. It increases cognitive load in situations where players should be focusing on core mechanics such as aim, positioning, and teamwork.\n\nRather than evolving player intuition, the system disrupts it, creating frustration without offering a clear or rewarding alternative.\n\nIf the goal is to add depth, there are more balanced approaches:\n- Allow partial ammo retention instead of complete loss  \n- Increase magazine availability  \n- Consider limiting this system to non-competitive modes  \n\nAt its current state, the change adds friction, but not meaningful depth.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.	t	6825	koreana	2026-03-11 09:17:49	2026-06-04 09:16:03.336455
